Subject: [PATCH] cgroup, sched: add KMI-compatible CPU and PID limits for 5.10.272

Target baseline: Android common android12-5.10-lts, 8059ae219630 (5.10.272)
Source repository: https://github.com/OneFeiFan/gki-kernel-5.10-xiaomi-pad6max
Source revision: 7737c7f646063a874016b6fc04828d89befff904

Combine the following patches by OneFeiFan, preserving their code and
configuration changes:
  patches/01-container/0004-cgroup-devices-pids-net-cls-perf.patch
  patches/10-sched/0027-cfs-bandwidth-kabi.patch

Enable CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH, CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS, CONFIG_CGROUP_DEVICE,
CONFIG_CGROUP_PERF, and CONFIG_CGROUP_NET_CLASSID in gki_defconfig.
The cgroup extension has exactly four slots and requires those four
controllers to be enabled together. It also relies on the target's stock
seven-controller configuration and specific arm64 structure offsets.
The scheduler uses task_group KABI reserve 2 and cfs_rq tail padding;
these locations must not be used by vendor code. Build-time assertions
check several, but not all, layout and configuration assumptions.

This is for a KMI frozen with these added options disabled. Do not apply
it to the source repository's source/ tree: those changes are already
present. A different kernel, configuration, compiler, or vendor module
set requires separate build, ABI/CRC and runtime verification.

Upstream credits: OneFeiFan; cgroup MAIN/EXT approach derived from
superturtlee/kernel-workshop-docker; CFS state split derived from
Droidspaces_Kernel_patch cgroup_limits/fix_cgroup_limits_kabi_5.15.167.patch.
Upstream reports testing on yudi 5.10.272, including a 20% CFS quota;
that report applies to the upstream build, not an independent test of this
extracted patch.

